id-grep
=======

id-grep is a local literature-search tool for infectious-disease ecology,
evolution, and epidemiology. It is a rebrand and redirection of `cs-grep`
toward the infectious-disease domain; the license is unchanged (see LICENSE).

Upstream lineage
----------------
- Derived from cs-grep by Philipp Normann — https://github.com/philippnormann/cs-grep
  (itself originally a security-focused tool, "sec-grep").

Data sources
------------
id-grep queries and attributes the following services. Please respect each
provider's terms of use and rate limits, and set a contact email where
requested (see `.env.example`).

- OpenAlex — https://openalex.org (primary ingestion; polite pool via OPENALEX_MAILTO)
- NCBI PubMed / E-utilities — https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK25501/
  (complementary ingestion; NCBI_API_KEY / NCBI_EMAIL)
- Crossref — https://www.crossref.org (abstract enrichment)
- Semantic Scholar — https://www.semanticscholar.org (abstract enrichment)
- DBLP — https://dblp.org (legacy computer-science ingestion, retained but unused
  by the default catalog)

Publisher abstract enrichment additionally fetches public landing pages
(PLOS, Elsevier, OUP, Royal Society, bioRxiv/medRxiv, CDC/EID, PNAS, Wiley)
subject to the tool's SSRF and size safeguards.
